# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ask Juice Doctor AI — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored) and fill in. Secrets are server-only and
# must never be committed. The app degrades to an honest "unavailable" state
# when a provider is not configured — it never fabricates AI answers or data.
#
# Every variable listed here is read by the codebase. The FINAL CONNECTION
# STAGE section lists providers whose application side is fully built: leave
# them unset and each surface shows an honest "not configured" state (see
# /admin/integrations); set them and the feature goes live — no code changes.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ══ REQUIRED for the live platform ═══════════════════════════════════════════

# Supabase (database + auth). URL + anon key are PUBLIC (safe in the browser);
# the service-role key is SERVER-ONLY (bypasses RLS) — never expose it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Anthropic Claude — powers the receptionist assessment, all specialist
# replies and the admin playground. SERVER-ONLY. Without it, AI features show
# an honest "AI unavailable" state.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Canonical origin (auth redirects, canonical/OG URLs, email links) —
# see NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL in the FINAL CONNECTION STAGE section below.

# ══ OPTIONAL — tuning & behaviour ════════════════════════════════════════════

# AI provider + model. Only "anthropic" is implemented; the provider
# abstraction lets another be added without rewriting the HERNE engine.
AI_PROVIDER=anthropic
# Default model (preferred over the legacy AI_MODEL, which is still honoured).
ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5
# AI_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Guardrails on every live call + durable per-user usage limits.
AI_MAX_INPUT_TOKENS=14000
AI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=1024
# Request timeout: milliseconds (>=1000) or seconds (<1000, scaled up).
AI_REQUEST_TIMEOUT=60000
AI_DAILY_USER_LIMIT=50
AI_MONTHLY_USER_LIMIT=500

# Reserved seam (src/services/index.ts): setting APP_MODE=production selects
# database-backed marketing-content providers once client-approved copy moves
# into the database. Leave unset until then — unset keeps the file-based
# placeholder marketing content (pending client-supplied copy). Never gate
# secrets on this.
# APP_MODE=production

# ══ FINAL CONNECTION STAGE ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Application side complete for every provider below; each stays honestly
# "Not configured" (see /admin/integrations) until its credentials exist.

# ── Custom domain — canonical origin for links, canonical/OG URLs and auth
# redirects. Full fallback chain when unset: VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL,
# then VERCEL_URL, then http://localhost:3011 — so the Vercel production URL
# applies automatically until the final domain is set here.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=

# ── Email (Resend) + business addresses (Zoho mailboxes on the final domain).
# Without these, every send is recorded as blocked in the mail outbox and no
# surface ever claims an email was sent.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=
# MAIL_REPLY_TO_ADDRESS=
# CONTACT_INBOX_ADDRESS=
# STAFF_ALERTS_ADDRESS=

# ── Wearables (Thryve) — see docs/integrations/thryve.md. Like the payment
# provider, setting these alone does NOT activate the integration: the
# contract-specific Thryve adapter (one file, provider.ts) must be implemented
# from the official API docs at connection time. Until both exist, connections
# stay honestly unavailable and the webhook/callback answer 503.
# THRYVE_API_KEY=
# THRYVE_APP_ID=
# THRYVE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Voice — Deepgram (speech-to-text) + ElevenLabs (read-aloud). Voice
# controls state "not available yet" until set; per-specialist voice ids are
# configured on /admin/integrations.
# DEEPGRAM_API_KEY=
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# ELEVENLABS_DEFAULT_VOICE_ID=

# ── Monitoring — Sentry (server errors) and PostHog (content-free product
# events). Internal AI usage/cost/reliability analytics run regardless.
# SENTRY_DSN=
# POSTHOG_API_KEY=
# POSTHOG_HOST=https://eu.i.posthog.com

# ── Background jobs — shared secret for /api/jobs/run (Vercel Cron sends it
# automatically once set). The runner answers 503 until then.
# CRON_SECRET=

# ── Payments — provider undecided. Naming one here does nothing until its
# adapter is implemented behind src/lib/payments/provider.ts; payments remain
# manual admin records either way.
# PAYMENT_PROVIDER=

# ══ OPERATOR TOOLING ONLY (read by no code in this repository) ═══════════════

# Supabase Management API token (sbp_…) + project ref — held here for the
# operator's external migration/key-management tooling (Supabase CLI,
# Management API calls). Nothing in this repository — runtime or scripts —
# reads them; the bootstrap script uses the runtime Supabase variables above.
SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=
